  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerated Education Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Somalia):  Basic education is the foundation for increased access to economic, social, and political opportunities and broader resilience to withstand al-Shabaab&apos;s ideological attacks and coercive recruitment techniques. The Accelerated Education Activity will provide accelerated basic education and non-formal education for out-of-school children and youth between the ages of 12 to 25. The activity will target 17 districts, prioritizing marginalized areas of south and central Somalia. This activity has four expected results: 1) increase equitable access to accelerated basic education and non-formal education programs; 2) improve learning outcomes in foundational skills areas (such as literacy, numeracy, and social-emotional learning); 3) increase community engagement and local ownership of accelerated and non-formal education programming; and 4) strengthen the capacity of government at local and federal levels to oversee the provision of quality public education..With FY 2024 funds, the activity will revise and distribute learning materials developed for accelerated basic education and non-formal learners to complement the government&apos;s formal curriculum. USAID will partner with federal- and state-level education ministries to provide in-service training for teachers and assist the government and the private sector to develop programming and policies on teacher qualifications, instructional time, and academic standards. This latter effort will lead to accreditation  and certification of students so that they may transition into formal schools at the right level. To promote inclusion, the activity will foster positive gender norms, implement safe learning environment standards, and reduce educational barriers for girls and boys. This activity will also be &quot;shock responsive,&quot; able to pivot programming to provide critical education support in the event that target populations are displaced by droughts, floods, or conflict..... .. .....</narrative>
  </description>
